---
// Draft: the leading underscore keeps Astro from building this page until the owner approves publication.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Vocabulary sync" description="Keep your SonoJot vocabulary on your devices with free, end-to-end encrypted sync." noindex>
 <Nav/>
 <main id="main" class="column stock sync-page" data-text-surface="flat">
  <p class="eyebrow">Vocabulary sync · DRAFT staging preview</p>
  <h1>Your words, on your devices.</h1>
  <p class="lead">Add a name once. Keep it in your vocabulary wherever you use SonoJot. Vocabulary sync is free.</p>
  <h2>Only your devices can read it</h2>
  <p>Your computer encrypts your vocabulary before it leaves. Your other devices unlock it with keys they hold. Signing in identifies your account; it does not give SonoJot, your sign-in provider or our hosting provider the keys.</p>
  <h2>Bring another device</h2>
  <p>Choose Set up sync and create your account with an email code. SonoJot creates the encryption key on your computer; save your recovery code once. On another computer, choose Add this computer, sign in with the same email, and compare six digits on both screens. Confirm the match on both computers.</p>
  <h2>Save your recovery code</h2>
  <p>Keep it in your password manager or another safe place. If every device is lost, sign in and enter the recovery code to unlock your words. If you lose the code too, no one can recover the synced copy. Starting over requires a 72-hour wait, during which an unlocked device can cancel.</p>
  <h2>What syncs?</h2>
  <p>Your vocabulary entries, including their kind. Learned suggestions stay on the device until you add them to vocabulary. This stage does not sync meetings or audio.</p>
  <h2>What can the Studio see?</h2>
  <p>Your account email, sign-in identity, device platforms, sync times and encrypted object sizes. Our identity provider handles sign-in and sees your email and sign-in metadata, including browser and device signals used to prevent abuse. It receives no vocabulary or encryption key. The service cannot decrypt your vocabulary without a key from your devices or recovery code. This assumes your devices and the app itself are trustworthy and you compare pairing codes on both screens. Sign-in email changes cannot redirect reset notices without confirmation from an unlocked app. Provider deletion or revocation does not erase encrypted sync or prevent a key-holding device from cancelling a reset. The account page shows metadata; device removal and deletion require an unlocked app.</p>
  <h2>What if I lose a device?</h2>
  <p>Remove it from Account and sync in an unlocked app; removal re-keys by default, and save the new recovery code. Your other computers pick up the new key on their next sync. If a computer cannot verify the key change, compare six digits again or use the newest recovery code. Removal cannot erase old copies or keys. A malicious server working with a removed device could hide the change from an offline device still using old keys; automatic verification establishes the new keys when the change arrives; pairing is needed if its trust history is missing.</p>
  <h2>Can I keep everything local?</h2>
  <p>Yes. Sync is optional. SonoJot still works without an account. You can also configure an HTTPS self-hosted sync server in Account and sync.</p>
  <p class="availability">This preview is for staging review. Public sign-in and launch await setup and approval. Open Settings → Account and sync in a staging build to test.</p>
 </main><Footer/>
</Base>
